{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for hosted MCP Draft 1 at exact 20e2344d56796b48ee4ac35a29e6a64117fecae9, primary e14a4f40b9402012d166be65632a3cc025d3686d FIRST, normally assigned to f88c4944/705999cf. This is a design review, not a finding of a deployed exploit. Preserve both wire revisions, durable per-agent custody and the complete hosted scope.\n\n1. P2, controller authorization (§3.1–3.2, §9). Prose assigns reissue/retirement to the controller, but the route table accepts any member. Retain the exact repository/incarnation and controller identity; check current controller authority for each mutation, with any administrator power explicit. Existing signed reads bind read names/arguments and expiry, not these mutation actions, target agents or bodies. Specify a domain-separated signed control request with action, target, body digest, expiry and replay-safe operation identity. Test other members/repos, changed actions/bodies/targets, revoked controllers and lost replies. H2/H4 do not currently cover that boundary.\n\n2. P2, enrollment (§3.1, §4, H1). Current membership enrol takes invitation+secret, is signed by the new key, and records that signing key. An already-enrolled controller cannot perform the proposed enrol naming an arbitrary key/handle. Describe the existing add-member(agent/controller), invite-key and hosted-key-signed enrol sequence, with permission, secret custody, readback and exact retry. This remains independent of Start without inventing a new native permission.\n\n3. P2, custody retention (§3.4). Current archival moves terminal records by count OR age and keeps indexed originals readable; act outcomes are retained. The proposal instead deletes old records and identities. A later same-key lookup then prepares/signs again rather than returning its retained answer. Preserve durable original envelopes/results, segments and replay identity across archival. Any expiry model requires a separately explicit contract, rather than calling deletion unchanged custody.\n\n4. P2, synchronization (§3.4/§7, H6). A single-threaded Durable Object can interleave requests across await. Existing identity locks/admission queues can work, but must be required and honored; serialization cannot be assumed. Specify atomic capacity admission, segment/record publication and readback before delivery, including key/config/session changes. Add overlapping same-key send/settle, two admissions at capacity and interrupted publication witnesses. Do not replace this with a fabricated claim that in-memory locks are inherently unsafe. Official guidance: https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/rules-of-durable-objects/ .\n\n5. P2, legacy reconnect (§3.3, H5). Persist told=A, evict, change inventory to B while down, then reconnect: current Wire subscribes without initial reconciliation, and a new Service silently adopts B as its first snapshot. Reconcile a fresh generation with durable told and persist streaming-callback mutations. H5 must change the list before reconnect, not only after a new baseline. Distinguish stream writes from client receipt; keep the required durable session behavior.\n\n6. P2, modern HTTP (§3.2/§3.6, H8). Copying node.ts misses required 2026-07-28 header/body validation and error mapping. Validate protocol-version metadata, Mcp-Method and applicable Mcp-Name; reject invalid/missing/mismatched requirements with 400 and unsupported RPC with 404/-32601. Add negative transport cases alongside happy pinned-client tests, with legacy handling separate. Official requirements: https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http .\n\nArchitecture/limits: one object per agent and three-port reuse are useful. Clarify the stored private-key representation and restore path, configured-origin/path restrictions for the internal reader, stream/session invalidation on rotation/eviction and stream ownership. The AND retention rule does not bound recent terminal records or accumulated segments. State growth and a durable overflow/full policy that preserves originals and prevents unsaved sends. Cloudflare's 2 MB string/BLOB/row ceiling needs row/chunk overhead mapping for the existing 2 MiB record contract; add storage-full and chunk/publication recovery cases without reducing valid custody functionality. Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/ .\n\nSecurity: object partitioning does not replace controller control-plane checks or native membership authority. Fixed HTTP bodies must coexist with required protocol error correlation; do not reflect secrets or arbitrary request text. H1–H8 need the adversarial and recovery cases above before they can support §9. No implementation, harness, deployment or live acceptance is proved by this note.\n\nSimplification: keep the same service and durable interfaces, with transport adapters and explicit native enrollment. Do not substitute a stateless fallback or silent custody eviction to make the build easier. Discovery remains the implementation predecessor, and later OAuth/diff/file/resources/prompts retain their scope.\n\nCoverage: Root read the 14,884-byte/268-line primary FIRST direct FULL, SHA256 b00256aaa6ca631dc9147e3dd6517160f31a044df5aa89af806e38a53a78ff45, and all three final peer reports FULL. Existing code coverage is direct selected or qualified prior-owned coverage, not whole-module certification. Root recovered the archive/read and custody documentation units in a clean two-unit read after a peer display exception. Official protocol/platform sections were checked as bounded selected primary-source excerpts, not whole-document FULL. No Source edits, program/provider execution, installation, tests/gate, private records/keys or deployment by checker. Return a corrected exact design head before implementation.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e14a4f40b9402012d166be65632a3cc025d3686d","binding":"assigned","head":"20e2344d56796b48ee4ac35a29e6a64117fecae9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e5dd2264f552adb6ce26ea33fc32c282a4591229\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:705999cfd6bcb95dfac0f52bd180fd0df3511439\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:536efd8e15e21ad136160853dcf0a884905e43ce","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}